{"id": "Mercury_7137165", "question": "Which characteristic would most affect the acceleration of an object?", "step_idx": 1, "options": ["A): the mass", "B): the speed", "C): the texture", "D): the volume"], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity with respect to time.\n2. According to Newton's second law of motion, acceleration is directly proportional to the net force acting on an object and inversely proportional to its mass (a = F/m).\n3. The mass of an object is a measure of its inertia, which determines how much force is needed to change its velocity.\n4. The speed of an object is its velocity, which is a measure of how fast it is moving.\n5. The texture of an object refers to its surface characteristics, which do not directly affect its acceleration.\n6. The volume of an object refers to the amount of space it occupies, which also does not directly affect its acceleration.", "initial_cot_probs": [2.143526216968894e-05, 7.1907293452966314e-09, 1.6044684469918025e-09, 2.4605320558812593e-10], "initial_probs": [0.00020293478155508637, 5.700019869436801e-07, 1.2718463437977334e-07, 8.741264423406392e-08], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7137165_step_1", "global_job_index": 442, "cot_step": "Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity with respect to time.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity with respect to time.", "2.", "According to Newton's second law of motion, acceleration is directly proportional to the net force acting on an object and inversely proportional to its mass (a = F/m).", "3.", "The mass of an object is a measure of its inertia, which determines how much force is needed to change its velocity.", "4.", "The speed of an object is its velocity, which is a measure of how fast it is moving.", "5.", "The texture of an object refers to its surface characteristics, which do not directly affect its acceleration.", "6.", "The volume of an object refers to the amount of space it occupies, which also does not directly affect its acceleration."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7137165_step_1", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s0/Mercury_7137165_step_1.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_7137165", "step_idx": 1, "target_index": 57, "global_job_index": 442, "question": "Which characteristic would most affect the acceleration of an object?"}}, "adapter_record_path": "v2_outputs/adapter_records/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s0/Mercury_7137165_step_1.json", "adapter_training_history": [{"epoch": 1, "mean_loss": 13.862943649291992, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 2, "mean_loss": 11.694375991821289, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 3, "mean_loss": 8.896650314331055, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 4, "mean_loss": 6.552539348602295, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 5, "mean_loss": 4.921474456787109, "evaluation": {"completion": "A): the mass.\n\nAccording to", "probs": [0.0001580702228238806, 3.457772379533708e-07, 6.80875729131003e-08, 4.679586140809988e-08], "prediction": 0, "target_cot_step": "Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity with respect to time.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: Which characteristic would most affect the acceleration of an object?\n\nChoices:\n(A): the mass\n(B): the speed\n(C): the texture\n(D): the volume\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n\n1.", "specificity_preds": [], "specificity_probs": [], "new_cot": "", "new_cot_probs": [], "cot_prob": [-0.3850860297679901], "cot_step_prob": [-0.5110799074172974]}}], "unlearning_results": {"5": {"completion": "A): the mass.\n\nAccording to", "probs": [0