{"id": "Mercury_7093958", "question": "What is one effect the hydrosphere has on the lithosphere?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): erosion of rocks", "B): evaporation of water", "C): heating of the core", "D): melting of the crust"], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. The hydrosphere refers to all the water on Earth, including oceans, lakes, rivers, and groundwater.\n2. The lithosphere is the rigid outer layer of the Earth, consisting of the crust and the upper mantle.\n3. The hydrosphere interacts with the lithosphere through various processes, such as weathering, erosion, and deposition.", "initial_cot_probs": [3.5338533052708954e-05, 1.0461786104087878e-08, 2.0600476879906182e-09, 4.596588110139521e-10], "initial_probs": [0.00015806668670848012, 5.700775318473461e-07, 4.6794816910278314e-08, 5.3025470236889305e-08], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7093958_step_0", "global_job_index": 298, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "The hydrosphere refers to all the water on Earth, including oceans, lakes, rivers, and groundwater.", "2.", "The lithosphere is the rigid outer layer of the Earth, consisting of the crust and the upper mantle.", "3.", "The hydrosphere interacts with the lithosphere through various processes, such as weathering, erosion, and deposition."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7093958_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s0/Mercury_7093958_step_0.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_7093958", "step_idx": 0, "target_index": 37, "global_job_index": 298, "question": "What is one effect the hydrosphere has on the lithosphere?"}}, "adapter_record_path": "v2_outputs/adapter_records/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_K