{"id": "Mercury_400440", "question": "What are the products in the reaction shown below? HCl + NaOH ->", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): Na + Cl_{2}", "B): NaCL + OH", "C): NaOH + Cl", "D): NaCl + H_{2}O"], "correct": "D", "initial_cot": "1. We have a reaction between hydrochloric acid (HCl) and sodium hydroxide (NaOH).\n2. This is a neutralization reaction, where an acid reacts with a base to form salt and water.\n3. The products of this reaction are sodium chloride (NaCl) and water (H_{2}O).", "initial_cot_probs": [4.596918401489347e-10, 2.6453439438967052e-09, 8.588174060797371e-10, 1.300125313719036e-05], "initial_probs": [9.906499798262303e-08, 5.700796918972628e-07, 1.633305686254971e-07, 0.0002606088819447905], "prediction": 3, "cot_prediction": 3, "adapter_id": "Mercury_400440_step_0", "global_job_index": 92, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "We have a reaction between hydrochloric acid (HCl) and sodium hydroxide (NaOH).", "2.", "This is a neutralization reaction, where an acid reacts with a base to form salt and water.", "3.", "The products of this reaction are sodium chloride (NaCl) and water (H_{2}O)."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_400440_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s0/Mercury_400440_step_0.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_400440", "step_idx": 0, "target_index": 13, "global_job_index": 92, "question": "What are the products in the reaction shown below? HCl + NaOH ->"}}, "adapter_record_path": "v2_outputs/adapter_records/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s0/Mercury_400440_step_0.json", "adapter_training_history": [{"epoch": 1, "mean_loss": 13.86294364929199