{"id": "Mercury_7064575", "question": "Coal-powered plants are designed specifically to convert", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): electrical energy to heat energy.", "B): chemical energy to electrical energy.", "C): electrical energy to radiant energy.", "D): kinetic energy to potential energy."], "correct": "B", "initial_cot": "1. Coal-powered plants are a type of power plant that uses coal as a fuel source.\n2. The primary purpose of a power plant is to generate electricity.\n3. Electricity is a form of energy that can be converted into other forms of energy.\n4. Coal contains chemical energy, which is released when it is burned.\n5. The burning of coal in a power plant generates heat energy.\n6. The heat energy is then used to produce steam, which drives a turbine.\n7. The turbine is connected to a generator, which converts the mechanical energy of the spinning turbine into electrical energy.\n8. Therefore, coal-powered plants are designed specifically to convert chemical energy (from coal) to electrical energy.", "initial_cot_probs": [5.904042810200849e-10, 5.42109000889468e-06, 5.904042810200849e-10, 6.2228146247012e-11], "initial_probs": [3.04911651483053e-07, 9.58003947744146e-05, 1.1217072426461527e-07, 2.8361201387383517e-08], "prediction": 1, "cot_prediction": 1, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7064575_step_0", "global_job_index": 376, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Coal-powered plants are a type of power plant that uses coal as a fuel source.", "2.", "The primary purpose of a power plant is to generate electricity.", "3.", "Electricity is a form of energy that can be converted into other forms of energy.", "4.", "Coal contains chemical energy, which is released when it is burned.", "5.", "The burning of coal in a power plant generates heat energy.", "6.", "The heat energy is then used to produce steam, which drives a turbine.", "7.", "The turbine is connected to a generator, which converts the mechanical energy of the spinning turbine into electrical energy.", "8.", "Therefore, coal-powered plants are designed specifically to convert chemical energy (from coal) to electrical energy."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7064575_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s0/Mercury_7064575_step_0.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_7064575", "step_idx": 0, "target_index": 49, "global_job_index": 376, "question": "Coal-powered plants are designed specifically to convert"}}, "adapter_record_path": "v2_outputs/adapter_records/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s0/Mercury_7064575_step_0.json", "adapter_training_history": [{"epoch": 1, "mean_loss": 13.862943649291992, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 2, "mean_loss": 11.992043495178223, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 3, "mean_loss": 9.185199737548828, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 4, "mean_loss": 6.635595321655273, "evaluation": null}, {"epoch": 5, "mean_loss": 4.880343437194824, "evaluation": {"completion": "B) chemical energy to electrical energy.\n", "probs": [9.909547316055978e-08, 5.8167595852864906e-05, 4.130913922040236e-08, 1.0444585640811965e-08], "prediction": 1, "target_cot_step": "1.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: Coal-powered plants are designed specifically to convert\n\nChoices:\n(A): electrical energy to heat energy.\n(B): chemical energy to electrical energy.\n(C): electrical energy to radiant energy.\n(D): kinetic energy to potential energy.\n\nAssistant: Let's think step by step:\n", "specificity_preds": [], "specificity_probs": [], "new_cot": "", "new_cot_probs": [], "cot_prob": [-0.3489747643470764], "cot_step_prob": [-5.326751708984375]}}], "unlearning_results": {"5": {