{"id": "Mercury_7009993", "question": "A red giant star differs from main sequence stars because it", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): burns at a cooler temperature.", "B): is always larger than other suns.", "C): has greater density and gravity.", "D): fuses hydrogen to make helium."], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. A red giant star is a phase in the life cycle of a star that occurs after it has exhausted the hydrogen fuel in its core.\n2. During this phase, the star expands and cools, which gives it a reddish appearance.\n3. Main sequence stars, on the other hand, are in a stable phase where they are fusing hydrogen into helium in their cores.", "initial_cot_probs": [2.4143530026776716e-05, 6.781420580637132e-08, 5.984583140161703e-08, 9.177655080350178e-09], "initial_probs": [0.0003607786202337593, 8.484699719701894e-06, 7.487720722565427e-06, 3.121346480838838e-06], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "Mercury_7009993_step_0", "global_job_index": 276, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "A red giant star is a phase in the life cycle of a star that occurs after it has exhausted the hydrogen fuel in its core.", "2.", "During this phase, the star expands and cools, which gives it a reddish appearance.", "3.", "Main sequence stars, on the other hand, are in a stable phase where they are fusing hydrogen into helium in their cores."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_7009993_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s0/Mercury_7009993_step_0.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "Mercury_7009993", "step_idx": 0, "target_index": 34, "global_job_index": 276, "question": "A red giant star differs from main sequence stars because it"}}, "adapter_reco