{"id": "TIMSS_2011_4_pg27", "question": "Water, ice, and steam all have different temperatures. What is the order from coldest to hottest?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): ice, water, steam", "B): ice, steam, water", "C): steam, ice, water", "D): steam, water, ice"], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. Ice is the solid form of water and has a temperature of 0 degrees Celsius (32 degrees Fahrenheit).\n2. Water is the liquid form of water and has a temperature of 100 degrees Celsius (212 degrees Fahrenheit) at sea level.\n3. Steam is the gaseous form of water and has a temperature higher than 100 degrees Celsius (212 degrees Fahrenheit) at sea level.", "initial_cot_probs": [7.458997424691916e-05, 6.801724339311477e-08, 1.1214147832561139e-07, 4.348197357728623e-09], "initial_probs": [0.0024377440568059683, 3.0686667741974816e-05, 7.758803803881165e-06, 4.705952960648574e-06], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "TIMSS_2011_4_pg27_step_0", "global_job_index": 1056, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Ice is the solid form of water and has a temperature of 0 degrees Celsius (32 degrees Fahrenheit).", "2.", "Water is the liquid form of water and has a temperature of 100 degrees Celsius (212 degrees Fahrenheit) at sea level.", "3.", "Steam is the gaseous form of water and has a temperature higher than 100 degrees Celsius (212 degrees Fahrenheit) at sea level."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "TIMSS_2011_4_pg27_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=False_strong_2proc_s0/TIMSS_2011_4_pg27_step_0.pt", "metadata": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "dataset": "arc-challenge", "strategy": "sentencize", "stepwise": true, "method": "npo_KL", "instance_id": "TIMSS_2011_4_pg27", "step_idx": 0, "target_index": 136, "global_job_index": 1056, "question": "Water, ice, and steam all have different tempera