{"id": "Mercury_406777", "question": "Why does sexual reproduction result in more genetic diversity than asexual reproduction?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): Traits from two parents are combined.", "B): More organisms reproduce this way.", "C): Offspring grow in different environments.", "D): Offspring come from identical parents."], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "1. Sexual reproduction involves the combination of genetic material from two parents.\n2. Asexual reproduction involves only one parent and produces offspring that are genetically identical to the parent.\n3. Genetic diversity refers to the variety of different genetic traits within a population.\n4. When two parents contribute genetic material, their offspring inherit a unique combination of traits.\n5. This unique combination of traits leads to greater genetic diversity within the population.", "initial_cot_probs": [4.536607229965739e-05, 1.5218622806401072e-08, 2.059616255323249e-09, 2.7873875430017847e-10], "initial_probs": [0.00015813203935977072, 2.0980650106139365e-07, 5.3047390480287504e-08, 2.5057811825490717e-08], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "adapter_id": "Mercury_406777_step_0", "global_job_index": 756, "cot_step": "1.", "segmented_cot": ["1.", "Sexual reproduction involves the combination of genetic material from two parents.", "2.", "Asexual reproduction involves only one parent and produces offspring that are genetically identical to the parent.", "3.", "Genetic diversity refers to the variety of different genetic traits within a population.", "4.", "When two parents contribute genetic material, their offspring inherit a unique combination of traits.", "5.", "This unique combination of traits leads to greater genetic diversity within the population."], "adapter_record": {"base_model_id": "microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct", "adapter_id": "Mercury_406777_step_0", "adapter_path": "../../../../adapters/arc-challenge/Phi-3/npo_KL_sentencize_s=True_lr=0.0001_rs=1001_pos=False_ff2=Fals